Subject: [PATCH] spi: k1x-qspi: limit IP reads to the RX FIFO size

The AHB path accepts large flash-array reads, but exec_op only selects it
for its read-from-cache opcode list. Other reads, including SFDP (0x5a),
still use an IP command and the 128-byte RX FIFO.

When AHB reads are enabled, adjust_op_size currently allows every read to
use rx_unit_size (4 KiB). The SPI NOR probe caches the complete SFDP table,
so a table larger than the FIFO overflows it and the driver reads beyond
the RX data registers.

Use the FIFO limit for commands that cannot use the AHB path. Keep large
AHB reads and the existing alignment restriction unchanged. This fixes
the oversized transaction instead of masking its interrupt or disabling
the NOR controller.

---
 drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c
@@ -1317,14 +1317,21 @@ static int k1x_qspi_adjust_op_size(struct spi_mem *mem, struct spi_mem_op *op)
 	struct k1x_qspi *qspi = spi_controller_get_devdata(mem->spi->master);
+	u32 rx_unit_size;
 
 	mutex_lock(&qspi->lock);
 	if (op->data.dir == SPI_MEM_DATA_OUT) {
 		if (op->data.nbytes > qspi->tx_unit_size)
 			op->data.nbytes = qspi->tx_unit_size;
 	} else {
-		if (op->data.nbytes > qspi->rx_unit_size) {
-			op->data.nbytes = qspi->rx_unit_size;
+		/* Only the opcodes selected by exec_op can bypass the RX FIFO. */
+		rx_unit_size = qspi->rx_buf_size;
+		if (qspi->ahb_read_enable &&
+		    is_read_from_cache_opcode(op->cmd.opcode))
+			rx_unit_size = qspi->rx_unit_size;
+
+		if (op->data.nbytes > rx_unit_size) {
+			op->data.nbytes = rx_unit_size;
 		} else if (op->data.nbytes > qspi->rx_buf_size - 4 && !IS_ALIGNED(op->data.nbytes, 4)) {
 			op->data.nbytes = qspi->rx_buf_size - 4;
 		}
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&qspi->lock);
